/-
# Hall's verbal finiteness conjecture, relatively free case (Kourovka Notebook Problem 12.31)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 12.31 (S. V. Ivanov): for relatively free
groups `G`, prove or disprove P. Hall's conjecture: if a word `v` takes only finitely many values on
`G`, then the verbal subgroup `v(G)` is finite.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Basic.Finite.Defs
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Basic

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HallVerbalFinitenessRelativelyFreeKourovka12Problem31Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 12.31 (S. V.
Ivanov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700850 (`KOU-12.31`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A relatively free group is a group with a generating family every assignment of which extends to an
endomorphism (equivalently, a free group of the variety it generates), of arbitrary rank. A word is
an element of a free group of finite rank, its values on `G` are its images under all homomorphisms
to `G`, and `v(G)` is the subgroup generated by the values.
-/

/-- `G` is relatively free: it has a generating family `x` such that every assignment of the
generators extends to an endomorphism of `G` (equivalently, `G` is free on `x` in the variety it
generates). -/
def IsRelativelyFree (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ (ι : Type) (x : ι → G), Subgroup.closure (Set.range x) = ⊤ ∧
    ∀ y : ι → G, ∃ φ : G →* G, ∀ i, φ (x i) = y i

/-- The set of values of the word `v` on `G`. -/
def wordValues {n : ℕ} (v : FreeGroup (Fin n)) (G : Type*) [Group G] : Set G :=
  Set.range fun g : Fin n → G => FreeGroup.lift g v

/-- Kourovka 12.31 (S. V. Ivanov; P. Hall's conjecture for relatively free groups): if a word `v`
takes only finitely many values on a relatively free group `G`, then the verbal subgroup `v(G)`
is finite. -/
def relativelyFreeFiniteWordValuesFiniteVerbal : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsRelativelyFree G → ∀ (n : ℕ) (v : FreeGroup (Fin n)),
    (wordValues v G).Finite → (Subgroup.closure (wordValues v G) : Set G).Finite

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive records that the conjecture is disproved for relatively free
groups (A. Storozhev, 1996): some word takes only finitely many values on some relatively free group
whose verbal subgroup for that word is infinite. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.),
Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026),
Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 12.31 (S. V. Ivanov); resolution: A. Storozhev, Proc. Amer.
Math. Soc. 124 (1996), no. 10, 2953-2954, Kourovka Archive, Problem 12.31: the conjecture is
disproved.
-/
public theorem_wanted relativelyFreeFiniteWordValuesFiniteVerbal_refuted :
    ¬ relativelyFreeFiniteWordValuesFiniteVerbal

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HallVerbalFinitenessRelativelyFreeKourovka12Problem31Wanted
